  "seoBody": "<p>Most inspection and form apps are tools: the person on the job fills them in, and someone still writes the report. Quickler comes out of that write-up time. Graeme Clark at Ethos Safety went from 1 to 2 hours to 14 minutes on average. Here is when that matters, and when another tool is the better choice.</p><p>Quickler users cut desk time after the site visit by around 80%. It is £75 a month per phone number, with free dashboard accounts for everyone else, so set that against what an hour of that person's time costs you.</p><h2>What Quickler does differently</h2><ul><li><strong>You use WhatsApp.</strong> No new app to install. No login for the person on site.</li><li><strong>£75 per month per phone number & unlimited free dashboard accounts.</strong> Reports, the dashboard, sharing and downloads are free for everyone else. Paid accounts have no limits: reports, photos and messages are unlimited. Start with a 14-day free trial. Everything is unlocked and you need no card to start. Write 10 reports a month and that's £7.50 a report; at 30 a month it is £2.50 a report.</li><li><strong>Voice notes are written out.</strong> You can speak your answers.</li><li><strong>It fills in your own report.</strong> Send a finished one in Word or PDF and every new one comes back in that layout.</li></ul><h2>When Quickler suits you</h2><ul><li>You run the same kind of walk again and again.</li><li>You spend hours turning notes and photos into a report.</li><li>You want to Pay for each phone number on the account.</li></ul><h2>When another tool is better</h2><p>You need scheduling, quoting and invoicing in one place: look at SimPro, Joblogic or Fergus. You want one platform with training and assets as well: look at Mitti, formerly SafetyCulture. You need many UK certificate formats or full fleet management: use a dedicated tool.</p>",
